You are debugging a production issue where an e-commerce order service fails to roll back database operations when `OrderProcessingException` (a checked exception) is thrown during execution.

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processOrder(OrderRequest request) throws OrderProcessingException {
        Order order = new Order(request);
        orderRepository.save(order);

        if (!callExternalPaymentGateway(request)) {
            throw new OrderProcessingException("Payment gateway declined request");
        }
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an asynchronous notification component throws a `NullPointerException`, but your configured custom `AsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler` is never invoked. As a result, the exception disappears without any log traces or alert triggers.

java
@Component
public class NotificationService {

    @Async
    public CompletableFuture<Boolean> sendNotification(User user) {
        if (user.getEmail() == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("User email is required");
        }
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(true);
    }
}
